{"id": "unknown-2026-10-23-016", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yozma IN 11 review: The OG mini e-moto gets updates galore", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/image.png?w=1333\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>…including 4.5kW motor, bigger 1.4kWh battery and 45mph top speed</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yozma may not have invented the mini moto space, but they certainly helped mainstream it. Together with Tuttios and Sur Rons, <a href=\"https://electrek.co/2026/04/18/yozma-in10-review-1200-somehow-buys-a-40mph-ultra-capable-mini-electr", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/10/23/yozma-in-11-review-the-og-mini-e-moto-gets-updates-galore/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-23-017", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Overhead wired charging comes to Austin electric bus fleet", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/capital-projects-rapid.png?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">CapMetro’s Austin transit fleets electrified two public bus lines and opened two new park-and-ride facilities featuring overhead pantograph-style wired charging equipment to help Austinites breathe a little bit easier.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"austin,electric-buses,texas\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknow", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/10/23/overhead-wired-charging-comes-to-austin-electric-bus-fleet/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "tesla-2026-10-23-018", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["tesla"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tesla Q4 numbers, more product delays, and some REAL EV charging innovation", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/Tesla-HW3-overheat-fsd-v14-lite.webp.png?w=1248\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On today’s numerically-infused episode of <em><a href=\"https://youtu.be/YNN10jyCkMU\">Quick Charge</a></em>, we take a look at all the latest product and delivery delays from Tesla’s Q3 earnings call before changing lanes and recapping some of the biggest developments in the world of EV charging innovation.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/10/22/tesla-q4-numbers-more-product-delays-and-some-real-ev-charging-innovation/", "type": "rss"}]}
